with concerns over low water levels in  the colorado river a coalition is asking  federal officials and congress to do  more to protect our water source  lake mead is at a record low level and  dropping  hector mejia live in our newsroom with  possible help moving forward  hector makers and conservationists  called for a moratorium on dam  and diversion projects along the  colorado river that they said  are wasteful the group met at hoover dam  and live streamed their demands earlier  this morning  they specifically called out the  proposed lake powell pipeline in utah  they said the project would hurt nevada  and the other five western states that  rely on the colorado river for water  the pipeline would transport billions of  gallons of water  underground from northern arizona to  southwest utah  the utah rivers council a non-profit  that promotes  sustainability says it would further  deplete the river  and jeopardize our water source the lake  powell pipeline  would deliver water to some of america's  most wasteful water users  in washington county utah  water officials from all six states have  been critical of the project  though utah is entitled to that water  under state agreements made a century  ago  water officials from those states  including nevada have said they're  willing to negotiation  we'll keep you updated reporting in our  newsroom hector mejia 8 news now
 

